  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/benday-inc/Benday.CommandsFramework",
  "published": "2026-08-29T21:00:57.043Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.1 - First release. Adds the 'tui' keyword to any tool that references this package and calls .WithTui() on the CommandsApp builder; Browse the tool's commands grouped by category and nested by command group, with a fuzzy filter across names, aliases, categories and descriptions; Fill in a command's arguments in a form that picks its widget from the argument's own type, validates each value as it is typed without ever storing one the argument refuses, and reports what is wrong through the command's own validation; A live command line preview shows what the form adds up to, rendered in whichever argument syntax the tool accepts, with copy to clipboard; Run the command from the form and watch it work: its output streams into the pane with the result, status and error channels kept visually apart, progress is redrawn in place, a command that asks questions is prompted for them, and Ctrl-C cancels the command rather than the interface;",
